 "text": "Hi, how are you? Lots of left handed school friends use laptops on their laps for hours, and they're deeply unhappy about it. Perpendicular base on your lap is the big problem. It puts almost four kilograms of weight per hand on one small joint. Some lightweight convertible pads are worth looking for on light laptop. Many lefties switch one hand around, which works well up to a point. Some people also use a thin pad between the keyboard box and their skin, which helps a lot.",
